## Analysis: "Create-Snippet-from-Selection" Button Lifecycle in Inline Runner Footer

### Overview

The create-snippet-from-selection button is an icon button (`file-plus` icon) rendered inside the Inline Runner modal footer, to the right of the X close button. It is disabled by default and becomes enabled when the user selects text inside the runner's content area. Clicking it opens `SnippetEditorModal` pre-filled with the selected text. The entire feature was added in "Phase 2" and is fully self-contained within `InlineRunnerModal` — it has no test coverage and no external callers of its private methods.

---

### 1. Field Declaration (`src/views/inline-runner-modal.ts:79-81`)

Two private instance fields are declared right after `boundKeyHandler`:

```ts
// Line 79-81
/** Phase 2 — create-snippet-from-selection footer button + selection listener. */
private createSnippetBtnEl: HTMLButtonElement | null = null;
private boundSelectionHandler: (() => void) | null = null;
```

- `createSnippetBtnEl` holds a reference to the live `<button>` element so `updateCreateSnippetButtonState()` can toggle its `disabled` property.
- `boundSelectionHandler` stores the arrow-function wrapper so the exact same reference can be passed to both `addEventListener` and `removeEventListener` (required for successful detachment).

---

### 2. Listener Wiring in `open()` (`src/views/inline-runner-modal.ts:233-239`)

At the end of `open()`, after the `boundKeyHandler` is attached to `containerEl`, the selection listener is wired:

```ts
// Lines 233-239
// Phase 2 — track text selection inside contentEl to enable/disable the
// create-snippet-from-selection footer button. mouseup covers drag-selection;
// selectionchange covers keyboard Shift+Arrow selection.
this.boundSelectionHandler = () => this.updateCreateSnippetButtonState();
this.contentEl?.addEventListener('mouseup', this.boundSelectionHandler);
document.addEventListener('selectionchange', this.boundSelectionHandler);
```

Two listeners are registered:
- **`mouseup`** on `contentEl` — fires after drag-to-select with the mouse.
- **`selectionchange`** on `document` — fires for keyboard-based selection (Shift+Arrow). This is on `document` (not `contentEl`) because `selectionchange` does not bubble and must be on `document`.

Both point to the same `boundSelectionHandler` closure, which delegates to `updateCreateSnippetButtonState()`.

---

### 3. Footer Rendering in `render()` (`src/views/inline-runner-modal.ts:446-473`)

On every `render()` call, the footer button row is destroyed and recreated. The block at lines 446-473:

```ts
// Line 446-447
if (this.footerBtnRowEl !== null) {
  this.footerBtnRowEl.empty();  // destroys ALL children including close btn

  // Line 450-451 — left group div wraps close + create-snippet
  const leftGroup = this.footerBtnRowEl.createDiv({ cls: 'rp-runner-footer-left' });

  // Lines 453-457 — close button (always present)
  const closeBtn = leftGroup.createEl('button', { cls: 'rp-inline-runner-close-btn rp-runner-icon-btn' });
  setIcon(closeBtn, 'x');
  closeBtn.setAttribute('aria-label', this.plugin.i18n.t('protocolRunner.closeProtocol'));
  closeBtn.addEventListener('click', () => { this.close(); });

  // Lines 462-473 — create-snippet button
  const createSnippetBtn = leftGroup.createEl('button', {
    cls: 'rp-inline-runner-create-snippet-btn rp-runner-icon-btn',
    attr: { 'aria-label': this.plugin.i18n.t('protocolRunner.createSnippetFromSelection') },
  });
  setIcon(createSnippetBtn, 'file-plus');
  createSnippetBtn.disabled = true;
  createSnippetBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    void this.handleCreateSnippetFromSelection();
  });
  this.createSnippetBtnEl = createSnippetBtn;
  this.updateCreateSnippetButtonState();  // re-evaluate against live selection
}
```

Key observations:
- `footerBtnRowEl.empty()` destroys all children, so the close button **must** be recreated on every render — this is why both buttons live in the same block.
- The `leftGroup` div (`rp-runner-footer-left`) was introduced specifically for Phase 2 to wrap close + create-snippet buttons together on the left side of the `space-between` flex row. The `renderFooterIcons()` method (lines 535-573) separately appends the Back/Redo/Skip group (`rp-runner-footer-row`) to the right side.
- The create-snippet button starts `disabled = true` and is immediately re-evaluated via `updateCreateSnippetButtonState()` so that an existing selection at render time enables it.

**Removal impact**: After removing the create-snippet button, the `leftGroup` wrapper div becomes unnecessary — the close button can be created directly as a child of `footerBtnRowEl` (reverting to the pre-Phase-2 pattern used in `buildContainer()` at lines 358-364). Alternatively, the `leftGroup` could be retained with only the close button inside, but removing it is cleaner.

---

### 4. `getSelectedContentText()` (`src/views/inline-runner-modal.ts:739-755`)

```ts
private getSelectedContentText(): string {
  if (this.contentEl === null) return '';
  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return '';
  const sel = window.getSelection();
  if (sel === null || sel.isCollapsed) return '';
  const anchorNode = sel.anchorNode;
  if (anchorNode === null) return '';

  const contentEl = this.contentEl;
  let node: Node | null = anchorNode;
  while (node !== null) {
    if (node === contentEl) return sel.toString();
    node = node.parentNode;
  }
  return '';
}
```

This method walks the DOM tree upward from the selection's `anchorNode` to check whether the selection originates from within `contentEl`. If the anchor is inside the runner content, it returns the selection text; otherwise it returns `''` (e.g., if the user selected text in the note behind the runner). This prevents the button from enabling for selections outside the runner.

---

### 5. `updateCreateSnippetButtonState()` (`src/views/inline-runner-modal.ts:757-760`)

```ts
private updateCreateSnippetButtonState(): void {
  if (this.createSnippetBtnEl === null) return;
  this.createSnippetBtnEl.disabled = this.getSelectedContentText().length === 0;
}
```

Called on every `mouseup` and `selectionchange` event. Sets `disabled = true` when there is no in-content selection, `false` when there is one.

---

### 6. `handleCreateSnippetFromSelection()` (`src/views/inline-runner-modal.ts:762-775`)

```ts
private async handleCreateSnippetFromSelection(): Promise<void> {
  const template = this.getSelectedContentText();
  if (template.length === 0) return;
  const modal = new SnippetEditorModal(this.app, this.plugin, {
    mode: 'create',
    initialFolder: this.plugin.settings.snippetFolderPath,
    initialTemplate: template,
  });
  modal.open();
  await modal.result;
}
```

- Re-reads the selection (defensive — covers the disabled-button edge case).
- Constructs `SnippetEditorModal` in `create` mode with `initialTemplate` set to the selected text.
- Opens the modal and awaits its `result` promise. The inline runner stays visible underneath because `SnippetEditorModal` is an Obsidian `Modal` that mounts to `document.body` and stacks above the runner overlay.
- This is the **only** call site for `SnippetEditorModal` within `inline-runner-modal.ts`.

---

### 7. Cleanup in `close()` (`src/views/inline-runner-modal.ts:268-275`)

```ts
// Lines 268-275
// Phase 2 — detach selection listeners and release DOM refs (parity with boundKeyHandler).
// Runs BEFORE contentEl/containerEl are nulled below so removeEventListener still sees the node.
if (this.boundSelectionHandler !== null) {
  this.contentEl?.removeEventListener('mouseup', this.boundSelectionHandler);
  document.removeEventListener('selectionchange', this.boundSelectionHandler);
  this.boundSelectionHandler = null;
}
this.createSnippetBtnEl = null;
```

This block runs **before** `contentEl` and `containerEl` are nulled (which happens later at lines 308-317), ensuring `removeEventListener` on `contentEl` still sees the live DOM node. Both listeners are detached, both fields are nulled — no leaked listeners or stale DOM refs.

---

### CSS Classes to Remove (`src/styles/inline-runner.css`)

**1. `.rp-runner-footer-left`** — lines 341-347:
```css
/* Phase 2 — footer left group: close + create-snippet-from-selection, pushed to the
   space-between row's start side (Back/Redo/Skip group stays on the end side). */
.rp-runner-footer-left {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--size-4-2);
  justify-content: flex-start;
}
```
This class was introduced exclusively for Phase 2 to group the close + create-snippet buttons. After removal, if the `leftGroup` div is also removed from the render code, this CSS rule becomes dead and should be deleted. The close button will work fine as a direct child of `.rp-inline-runner-footer-btn-row` (which has `display: flex; justify-content: space-between`).

**2. `.rp-inline-runner-create-snippet-btn`** — This class has **no dedicated CSS rule** in the stylesheet. It relies entirely on the shared `.rp-runner-icon-btn` styles (lines 322-340) for its appearance. No CSS removal is needed for this class — it only appears in the TypeScript `cls` string at line 463. Removing it from the TS is sufficient.

**`.rp-runner-icon-btn:disabled` rule** — lines 350-356:
```css
.rp-runner-icon-btn:disabled,
.rp-runner-icon-btn:disabled:hover {
  opacity: 0.4;
  cursor: not-allowed;
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--text-muted);
}
```
This was added in Phase 2 but is described as **additive** — it also styles the disabled state of the Back/Redo/Skip buttons (set via `.disabled = true` in `renderFooterIcons()`). This rule should be **KEPT** since those buttons still use it.

---

### i18n Key (`protocolRunner.createSnippetFromSelection`)

- **`src/i18n/locales/en.json:313`**: `"createSnippetFromSelection": "Create snippet from selection"`
- **`src/i18n/locales/ru.json:313`**: `"createSnippetFromSelection": "Создать сниппет из выделения"`

This key is referenced **only** at `src/views/inline-runner-modal.ts:464` (the button's `aria-label`). After removal, this key becomes orphaned in both locale files and should be removed from both `en.json` and `ru.json`.

---

### SnippetEditorModal — Other Callers (DO NOT DELETE)

`SnippetEditorModal` has **three other active callers** that keep it alive:

1. **`src/main.ts:324-338`** — `handleCreateSnippet()` method:
   ```ts
