## Analysis: "Create-Snippet-from-Selection" Button Lifecycle in Inline Runner Footer

### Overview

The create-snippet-from-selection button is an icon button (`file-plus` icon) rendered inside the Inline Runner modal footer, to the right of the X close button. It is disabled by default and becomes enabled when the user selects text inside the runner's content area. Clicking it opens `SnippetEditorModal` pre-filled with the selected text. The entire feature was added in "Phase 2" and is fully self-contained within `InlineRunnerModal` — it has no test coverage and no external callers of its private methods.

---

### 1. Field Declaration (`src/views/inline-runner-modal.ts:79-81`)

Two private instance fields are declared right after `boundKeyHandler`:

```ts
// Line 79-81
/** Phase 2 — create-snippet-from-selection footer button + selection listener. */
private createSnippetBtnEl: HTMLButtonElement | null = null;
private boundSelectionHandler: (() => void) | null = null;
```

- `createSnippetBtnEl` holds a reference to the live `<button>` element so `updateCreateSnippetButtonState()` can toggle its `disabled` property.
- `boundSelectionHandler` stores the arrow-function wrapper so the exact same reference can be passed to both `addEventListener` and `removeEventListener` (required for successful detachment).

---

### 2. Listener Wiring in `open()` (`src/views/inline-runner-modal.ts:233-239`)

At the end of `open()`, after the `boundKeyHandler` is attached to `containerEl`, the selection listener is wired:

```ts
// Lines 233-239
// Phase 2 — track text selection inside contentEl to enable/disable the
// create-snippet-from-selection footer button. mouseup covers drag-selection;
// selectionchange covers keyboard Shift+Arrow selection.
this.boundSelectionHandler = () => this.updateCreateSnippetButtonState();
this.contentEl?.addEventListener('mouseup', this.boundSelectionHandler);
document.addEventListener('selectionchange', this.boundSelectionHandler);
```

Two listeners are registered:
- **`mouseup`** on `contentEl` — fires after drag-to-select with the mouse.
- **`selectionchange`** on `document` — fires for keyboard-based selection (Shift+Arrow). This is on `document` (not `contentEl`) because `selectionchange` does not bubble and must be on `document`.

Both point to the same `boundSelectionHandler` closure, which delegates to `updateCreateSnippetButtonState()`.

---

### 3. Footer Rendering in `render()` (`src/views/inline-runner-modal.ts:446-473`)

On every `render()` call, the footer button row is destroyed and recreated. The block at lines 446-473:

```ts
// Line 446-447
if (this.footerBtnRowEl !== null) {
  this.footerBtnRowEl.empty();  // destroys ALL children including close btn

  // Line 450-451 — left group div wraps close + create-snippet
  const leftGroup = this.footerBtnRowEl.createDiv({ cls: 'rp-runner-footer-left' });

  // Lines 453-457 — close button (always present)
  const closeBtn = leftGroup.createEl('button', { cls: 'rp-inline-runner-close-btn rp-runner-icon-btn' });
  setIcon(closeBtn, 'x');
  closeBtn.setAttribute('aria-label', this.plugin.i18n.t('protocolRunner.closeProtocol'));
  closeBtn.addEventListener('click', () => { this.close(); });

